The authors, designers, and main contributors to logos are listed below.
logos's copyright is held by these individuals and the affiliated
institutions at the time of their contributions (note that some authors have
had more than one affiliated institution).  See the file COPYING for details on
the copyright and licensing of logos.

The developers and authors of logos are:
	Andrew Reynolds, The University of Iowa, Amazon Web Services
	Abdalrhman Mohamed, Stanford University

The logos codebase contains some source code from the lean-smt project, which
is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.  The copyright of that code
is held by the lean-smt authors.  See the lean-smt repository at
https://github.com/ufmg-smite/lean-smt for details.

The calculus that logos checks is compiled from a Eunoia signature of the
Cooperating Proof Calculus maintained by the cvc5 project.  The copyright of
that signature is held by the cvc5 authors.  See the cvc5 repository at
https://github.com/cvc5/cvc5 for details.
